ld the lock" on the same buffer simultaneously: exclusion is already broken. When that happens, both submitters write the single shared `b_mxfs_sync_wait` boolean, whichever submits last wins, and both completions can end up calling `xfs_buf_relse()` — which is exactly the leak that inflates the semaphore further (self-reinforcing). The completion-routing fixes from prior sessions (sess6/8/9) all patched *which branch* a completion takes, but none fixed the fact that the routing can cause more `relse()` calls than there were lock acquisitions.

