## Session summary

**Major win: wedge#2a (the multi-week hang blocker) is fixed and proven.** Root-caused via live `/proc/kcore` inspection (computed struct offsets from the deployed `.ko`'s DWARF info via `gdb`, then read the live wedged buffer's kernel memory directly) that `b_sema.count` had drifted to 83 instead of 0/1 — a completion-routing bug (shared, overwritable `b_mxfs_sync_wait` boolean) let an unrelated concurrent submitter's completion double-`relse()` a buffer, permanently corrupting its lock's exclusion guarantee and letting future submitters race indefinitely. Fixed by replacing the boolean with additive per-submission credit counters (`b_mxfs_sync_waiters`) consumed by exactly one completion event, in `pal/linux/xfs_buf.c` + `xfs/xfs_buf.h`. Validated with a full clean 24-round 32-node/CAW run: **zero P-IOWAIT-STUCK, zero shutdowns, zero corruption** — the furthest any session in this multi-week saga has reached (prior attempts always wedged by round 7-14).

**New, different, shallower bug surfaced once wedge2a stopped masking it:** at round 18 of that same run, every one of the 32 nodes agreed a single directory entry (`node9_f1`, the directory's shortform-born first entry) was durably missing. This matches a well-documented, previously-unresolved bug class from ~19 days of prior investigation (`compiled-dirreuse-node1f1-double-block0-orphan`) involving directory-format-conversion races under concurrent multi-node writes, with a fully-designed but never-implemented fix (`docs/canonical_block0_fix_plan.md`).

**In progress at relay:** raised several diagnostic probe caps that were exhausting too early to give visibility into round 18+, rebuilt (srcversion `F3605E04F868F43B15C432F`), and launched an instrumented repro (`instr=1 dirwr=1`, smaller `DRC_NFILES=10`/`DRC_ROUNDS=40` for faster cycling) to catch this bug again with full diagnostic data. That run was healthy through round 8+ with zero failures when the relay boundary hit. Criteria are **not yet met** — full state, the historical mechanism analysis, and exact next steps are saved to ccmemory (`ccloop3e02-sess2-INPROGRESS-r18undercount-instrumented-repro-launched`) for continuation.

